059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436070 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436070 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436070 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436070 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436070 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436070 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c212f72a-279f-54ef-b120-28592cf65c59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436071 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436067 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436071 #edb/ref 1069 "q-97031" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436071 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436071 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{4},$ find $T(v).$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436071 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "132fd44c-38e5-5ebe-8c05-231eab1b1859" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436071 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436072 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436072 #edb/ref 1069 "q-8028" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436072 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436072 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the standard matrix that  represents  the  linear  transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z \\\\ x-y-z\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436072 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "43480c80-f56c-525c-8e3a-4535ddf6aa7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436072 #edb/ref 1074 "We require a $2\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2x+(-1)y+1z \\\\ 1x+(-1)y+(-1)z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z \\\\ x-y-z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436073 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436073 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96976" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436073 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436073 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\,T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}3y+ax \\\\ bx+4y \\\\ cy+3x\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ shown above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436073 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "93b16baf-60a0-5351-9b6d-e1dbecba8523" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436073 #edb/ref 1074 "Given the vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5x+3y \\\\ -2x+4y \\\\ 3x-y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3y+5x \\\\ -2x+4y \\\\ -y+3x\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}3y+5x \\\\ (-2)x+4y \\\\ (-1)y+3x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b+c=5+(-2)+(-1)=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436074 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436074 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140366" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436074 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436074 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{4},$ where\n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-4x-z+5y \\\\ 3x+7z-2y \\\\ -6x+y \\\\ 8y-3x\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436074 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d43f6aa4-a331-53b3-b9d7-aed1378d0872" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436074 #edb/ref 1074 "We require a $4\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}(-4)x+5y+(-1)z \\\\ 3x+(-2)y+7z \\\\ (-6)x+1y+0z \\\\ (-3)x+8y+0z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4x-z+5y \\\\ 3x+7z-2y \\\\ -6x+y \\\\ 8y-3x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
